# Per-package coverage floors for eka-core (read by scripts/coverage-gate.sh).
#
# A single module-wide number hides exactly the thing worth knowing: the
# package with the widest blast radius being the least tested. These floors
# exist so a regression in one package is visible instead of averaged away by
# the thirteen that are healthy.
#
# Each floor is set a little below the measured value so ordinary refactoring
# does not break the build, but a real drop does. Raising a floor when coverage
# improves is encouraged; lowering one is a deliberate decision, not a cleanup.
#
# Format: <package> <minimum-percent>
#
# The packages with the highest blast radius — metadata (every eka.yaml read),
# runtime (every lifecycle transition), store (the canonical store) — are the
# reason this file exists at all.
metadata             92
runtime              63
store                77
conformance          72
contexts             78
exchange             79
sync                 74
workspace            72
codegraph            66
compile              81
plugin               88
view                 86
machine              90
pathglob             90